{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Downlink Client Hint.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Downlink Client Hint.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"downlink client hint downlink client hint","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Downlink Client Hint.md","fileName":"Downlink Client Hint.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Downlink Client Hint","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-28 04:01\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Adaptive Image Delivery and Caching]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Adaptive Image Delivery and Caching","CDN Variant Cache Fragmentation","highperformanceimages.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Downlink Client Hint.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Downlink Client Hint.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"downlink client hint downlink client hint","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Downlink Client Hint.md","fileName":"Downlink Client Hint.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Downlink Client Hint","heading":"Downlink Client Hint","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"A downlink hint estimates the client’s available network throughput. An adaptive service can use a slower estimate to choose fewer bytes, a lower quality tier, or a more conservative resolution.\n\nNetwork estimates are transient and imperfect. They should influence graceful quality choices rather than determine whether meaningful content is delivered. Cache design also needs bounded buckets; varying on an effectively continuous value can destroy reuse. See [[CDN Variant Cache Fragmentation]].","tags":["baby"],"links":["Adaptive Image Delivery and Caching","CDN Variant Cache Fragmentation","highperformanceimages.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Downlink Client Hint.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Downlink Client Hint.md","